          "source_text_sha256": "5619a296dec2a3e4ea886a5cdce334b7966589b9caf7baec708dde7af38ad613",
          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "needs-review",
          "text": "Description: On June 6, 1983, around 11 PM, numerous witnesses across southern France, from the Alps to the Eastern Pyrenees, observed a rapidly moving light in the sky at the same time (11 PM) and for a short duration (most often less than 20 seconds, and at most 1 or 2 minutes). Twenty-nine testimonies have been reported. The shape is often described as elongated. The summary table (attached in the investigation elements) of observation locations and times is striking for its geographical scope and time correspondence. This supports a unique phenomenon produced at high altitude (> 50 km) and providing visibility over a large area. This is a key characteristic of the well-known atmospheric reentry phenomenon of a meteoroid. This is supported by another key characteristic, which is the elongated glow and short duration. A longer duration could have led to also considering the neighboring hypothesis regarding the atmospheric reentry of a space craft. In modern times, many sites record the data collected on the ground (most often by automatic cameras) during these reentries, such that reports of GEIPAN are resolved without particular investigation. The 2016 example with over 20 records (attached in the IMO supplementary analysis) illustrates the analogy with this old case of June 6, 1983 at 23:00. The supplementary analysis includes a collection of witness descriptions that clearly convey the impression of rapid movement with an elongated shape. As a result, the GEIPAN classifies the case as B: probable observations of atmospheric reentry of a meteoroid. A new testimony is added today: it concerns an observation made in Gémenos (13) around 23:00 of the rapid passage and disappearance of a yellow-white, elongated luminous phenomenon at low altitude. No noise was heard by the witness. Two press articles are attached to the completed questionnaire by the witness's spouse.",
